# Markdown assets (bootloader — spec in `docs/modules/md-format.md`, ADR-007)

## Invariants
- One `.md` = one whole asset: LaTeX (`$…$`, `$$…$$`) + base64 data-URI images; single-slot (`part_number` 1); filename `<QID>_<VERSION>_<ATYPE>.md`. Reorder is IMG-only.
- Sanitiser (`app/md_render.py`): `_BLEACH_PROTOCOLS` must include `data`; `_attr_allowed` is the real gate (`<img src>` only `data:image/*`; `<a href>` rejects `data:` / `javascript:` / `vbscript:`); markdown-it `html: False`. Changes here are security changes.
- Render cache: stat mtime **before** read, LRU 512, never cache errors; call `md_render.invalidate(path)` on every disk write (admin routes, smart import, copy/move).
- Editor concurrency: `mtime_ns` travels as a JSON **string**; `md/save` returns 409 `{current_mtime_ns}` unless `force`; `md/create` returns 409 `{existing_asset_id}` for an occupied slot.
- Editor UI: KaTeX preprocess before marked; empty `alt` on images; paste handler `stopPropagation`; fullscreen reparents to `<body>` and `destroy()` exits fullscreen first; no `maxHeight` inside modals. Factory returns `{easymde, getValue, setValue, getBytes, getMaxBytes, insertAtCursor, focus, refreshPreview, destroy}`.
- Generation: pandoc `--from=markdown+tex_math_dollars+tex_math_double_backslash-implicit_figures`; `_preprocess_md_for_pandoc` collapses blank lines inside `$$` and runs `normalize_inline_math`; literal dollars must be `\$`; Windows install-path fallbacks for `PANDOC_PATH`; failure → italic placeholder, generation continues.
- `MD_MAX_SIZE_BYTES` is a System Setting (group Markdown); `PANDOC_PATH` is `.env`-only.

## Gotchas
- AI "Generate Markdown" output follows `MD_FORMAT` (keep `[FIGURE: …]` markers) and `PDF_IMPORT_COORD_ORDER` for figure boxes.
- `migrate_md_format.py` is historical (enum widening now a boot patch) — do not run.
